{"id":"sea","name":"Sea","aliases":["Sea"],"sources":["nave","torrey","easton"],"topics":["nave:sea","torrey:sea-the"],"groups":["Symbolical"],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Sea, The","text":"(Heb. yam), signifies (1) “the gathering together of the waters,” the ocean (Gen. 1:10); (2) a river, as the Nile (Isa. 19:5), the Euphrates (Isa. 21:1; Jer. 51:36); (3) the Red Sea (Ex. 14:16, 27; 15:4, etc.); (4) the Mediterranean (Ex. 23:31; Num. 34:6, 7; Josh. 15:47; Ps. 80:11, etc.); (5) the “sea of Galilee,” an inland fresh-water lake, and (6) the Dead Sea or “salt sea” (Gen. 14:3; Num. 34:3, 12, etc.). The word “sea” is used symbolically in Isa. 60:5, where it probably means the nations around the Mediterranean. In Dan. 7:3, Rev. 13:1 it may mean the tumultuous changes among the nations of the earth."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H3220","lemma":"יָם","xlit":"yâm","gloss":"a sea or large body of water","kjv":"sea ), south, west","count":57,"share":0.47},{"strong":"G2281","lemma":"θάλασσα","xlit":"thálassa","gloss":"the sea","kjv":"sea","count":26,"share":0.22},{"strong":"H1530","lemma":"גַּל","xlit":"gal","gloss":"something rolled","kjv":"billow, heap, spring, wave","count":9,"share":0.07},{"strong":"H5104","lemma":"נָהָר","xlit":"nâhâr","gloss":"a stream","kjv":"flood, river","count":9,"share":0.07},{"strong":"H8064","lemma":"שָׁמַיִם","xlit":"shâmayim","gloss":"the sky","kjv":"air, astrologer, heaven","count":11,"share":0.09},{"strong":"H2344","lemma":"חוֹל","xlit":"chôwl","gloss":"sand","kjv":"sand","count":6,"share":0.05}],"verses":["Gen.1.10","Gen.1.22","Gen.14.3","Gen.22.17","Gen.49.13","Exod.10.19","Exod.13.18","Exod.20.11","Exod.23.31","Num.34.6","Num.34.12","Deut.3.17","Deut.11.24","Deut.33.19","Deut.34.2","1Kgs.4.29","Ezra.3.7","Job.6.3","Job.11.9","Job.38.8","Job.41.31","Ps.24.2","Ps.65.7","Ps.68.22","Ps.69.34","Ps.77.19","Ps.78.27","Ps.89.9","Ps.93.4","Ps.95.5","Ps.104.25","Ps.107.23","Ps.135.6","Prov.8.29","Eccl.1.7","Isa.5.30","Isa.11.9","Isa.11.15","Isa.4